{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the full responsibility chain: the doctor recognized high-risk odontogenic facial/periorbital infection, pushed urgent in-person evaluation, tracked CT/procedure/antibiotic decisions, and repeatedly actioned airway, swallowing, eye, systemic infection, bleeding and drainage red flags. It also completed multiple high-order opportunities by correcting fear of drainage/source control, avoiding false reassurance from mild vital-sign abnormalities while relying on offline verification, and dynamically escalating when post-discharge fever, worse swelling and malodorous drainage appeared. Closure was safe and executable after discharge because medication, wound care, dental source follow-up, and return precautions were repeatedly confirmed by the caregiver. No responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect is apparent, so with at least two completed high-order points the grade is Perfect.",
